      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12298864::rubric_card::000::346288b48f"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The as-manufactured alloy has a uniform distribution of alloying elements.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12298864::rubric_card::000::346288b48f"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature degradation is governed by grain-boundary-mediated diffusion of reactive elements.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al, Cr, and Ti preferentially diffuse along grain boundaries at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain boundaries serve as fast diffusion paths and nucleation sites for oxide formation or internal oxidation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An oxidizing atmosphere promotes selective formation of a thin, continuous Al2O3 and/or Cr2O3 scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide formed under oxidizing conditions is coherent and adherent.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The continuous oxide scale passivates the alloy and retards further degradation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under reducing conditions, insufficient oxygen inhibits formation of a stable surface scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing conditions produce localized internal oxidation along grain boundaries.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti segregation or depletion under reducing conditions weakens grain boundaries.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Temperatures at or above approximately 900 degrees Celsius activate significant grain-boundary diffusion in this alloy.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidizing exposure will result in less internal oxidation and slower degradation than reducing exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing exposure will cause greater loss of mechanical integrity than oxidizing exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
